        "title": "Ask wo for a fixed location",
        "body": "Use **wo** when you want to know where a place is. German puts the conjugated verb directly after the question word: **Wo ist die Post?** English adds “is” in the same kind of question, but does not use “do.”\n\nFor a short route answer, **links**, **rechts**, and **geradeaus** can stand alone. To describe distance, use **nahe** with **sein**: **Die Bank ist nahe.**",
        "examples": [
          { "target": "Wo ist der Bahnhof?", "source": "Where is the train station?" },
          { "target": "Die Post ist rechts.", "source": "The post office is on the right." },
          { "target": "Das Hotel ist nahe.", "source": "The hotel is nearby." }
        ]
      },
