      "tip": {
        "title": "Time first still means verb second",
        "body": "Like **können**, the modals **wollen** and **müssen** send the action infinitive to the end: **Ich will anfangen.** and **Wir müssen gehen.** English keeps the action beside “want to” or “must,” but German separates them.\n\nA time phrase can come first for emphasis. The conjugated verb must still be the second element, so the subject follows it: **Am Montag will ich anfangen.** Use **am** with days and **um** with clock times.",
        "examples": [
          { "target": "Am Montag will ich anfangen.", "source": "I want to start on Monday." },
          { "target": "Wir müssen um zehn Uhr gehen.", "source": "We have to go at ten o'clock." },
